WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:05.032
On Monday Daisy walked to school with Kaleem.

2
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:12.784
Beatrice flew along with them.

3
00:00:12.785 --> 00:00:16.658
When they reached the building, Beatrice looked nervous.

4
00:00:16.659 --> 00:00:25.241
"I don't think I should go inside," she said. "Too many people."

5
00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:31.004
Daisy nodded. "Why don't you stay outside until school ends?"

6
00:00:31.005 --> 00:00:39.121
"See you later!" Beatrice zipped off.

7
00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:49.037
Daisy was surprised to see her classmates in the hallway outside their classroom.

8
00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.998
"Good morning, students," their teacher said. "I have a surprise."

9
00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:58.809
"Did you outlaw homework?" Parker asked.

10
00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:06.317
Mr. Neal chuckled. "Nope. We have new class pets!"

11
00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:08.700
He flung open the door.

12
00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:15.439
From inside the room, Daisy heard dozens of tiny, chirping voices.

13
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.079
"What's going on?"

14
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.659
"This place is too small!"

15
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.324
"Let us out!"

16
00:01:22.325 --> 00:01:28.048
"Oh no!" Daisy thought. "Those poor crickets!"

17
00:01:28.049 --> 00:01:34.642
The students rushed over to the glass tank of crickets.

18
00:01:34.643 --> 00:01:38.361
"It'll be interesting to observe them," Mr. Neal said.

19
00:01:38.362 --> 00:01:42.245
Daisy shook her head. "The crickets are awake now.

20
00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:44.828
But crickets are mostly nocturnal.

21
00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:48.627
They probably won't be very interesting to watch during the day."

22
00:01:48.628 --> 00:01:56.189
"So?" Parker tapped on the tank.

23
00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.893
"We'll keep them awake."

24
00:01:58.894 --> 00:02:02.811
Daisy frowned. "That's mean!"

25
00:02:02.812 --> 00:02:04.864
Parker rolled his eyes.

26
00:02:04.865 --> 00:02:09.676
"Only a birdbrain like you cares about being nice to bugs."

27
00:02:09.677 --> 00:02:14.392
"Don't insult your classmate, Parker," Mr. Neal said sharply.

28
00:02:14.393 --> 00:02:17.866
"And don't worry, Daisy. The crickets will be fine."

29
00:02:17.867 --> 00:02:20.653
"But they won't be fine," Daisy said.

30
00:02:20.654 --> 00:02:22.458
"Maybe we should let them out."

31
00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:27.923
"What? No!" Raj, Parker's best friend, said.

32
00:02:27.924 --> 00:02:34.099
"We haven't had a class pet all year. And I thought you liked animals."

33
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:38.439
"I do," Daisy said. "We could get a different pet.

34
00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:44.250
Maybe fish, or another animal that doesn't mind being trapped in a small space."

35
00:02:44.251 --> 00:02:47.291
"Sit down, kids," Mr. Neal said.

36
00:02:47.292 --> 00:02:51.010
"It's time to start class."

37
00:02:51.011 --> 00:02:54.273
All morning Daisy had trouble concentrating.

38
00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.749
The crickets talked nonstop.

39
00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.579
"This place is too crowded!"

40
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.176
"Let's escape!"

41
00:03:03.177 --> 00:03:08.447
"I don't like it here."

42
00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:12.141
Finally it was time for recess.

43
00:03:12.142 --> 00:03:17.104
On her way out, Daisy stopped by the tank.

44
00:03:17.105 --> 00:03:19.834
"Sorry, crickets," she whispered.

45
00:03:19.835 --> 00:03:21.672
"I'll try to fix this."

46
00:03:21.673 --> 00:03:26.542
"Thank you!" the crickets chirped loudly.

47
00:03:26.543 --> 00:03:29.338
Kaleem was digging through his desk.

48
00:03:29.339 --> 00:03:31.896
Daisy was going to wait for him.

49
00:03:31.897 --> 00:03:35.976
But then she noticed Grace heading outside.

50
00:03:35.977 --> 00:03:38.895
She ran to catch up.

51
00:03:38.896 --> 00:03:42.789
"Have you heard how Mrs. Ortiz is doing?" Daisy asked.

52
00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.009
Grace shook her head.

53
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:49.276
"After we walked Scamp last night, my mom called to check on her.

54
00:03:49.277 --> 00:03:52.022
She's still in the hospital.

55
00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:58.286
She asked if we could take care of Scamp for a few more days. Is that okay?"

56
00:03:58.287 --> 00:04:02.413
"Of course," Daisy said. "It's hot today.

57
00:04:02.414 --> 00:04:05.861
We should make sure his pool is full of water."

58
00:04:05.862 --> 00:04:09.389
Grace nodded. "My dad works from home.

59
00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.605
He's going to walk him at lunchtime.

60
00:04:11.606 --> 00:04:14.056
We can check on him after school."

61
00:04:14.057 --> 00:04:18.743
Kaleem hurried over. "Want to play soccer?

62
00:04:18.744 --> 00:04:29.391
But watch out—I learned a new way to juggle the ball!"

63
00:04:29.392 --> 00:04:34.367
The three of them played soccer until recess was over.

64
00:04:34.368 --> 00:04:42.583
Then they went inside with the rest of the class.

65
00:04:42.584 --> 00:04:46.318
When they got there, Daisy gasped.

66
00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:49.848
The glass tank was lying on its side.

67
00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:57.906
"Oh no!" Grace whispered. "The crickets are loose!"

